  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 257 AM EDT Mon Jun 29 2026\n\n\n- Non-zero chance for storms this morning\n\nStill the potential for a few lightning strikes from the showers\ncurrently over the area. The showers currently over Michigan give\nour southern and eastern zones their best shot for rain/thunder\nthis morning.\n\nThe northern zones best chance comes from whether or not showers/storms\ncurrently developing over Wisconsin make a southerly/southeasterly\nturn and make it across Lake Michigan. Still enough instability to\nkeep us in the marginal risk for severe weather - with greatest\nrisk for hail and damaging winds. Models have all backed off \nsomewhat on bringing anything into the area at all...keeping\ndecaying storms in northern Lower...so this morning could also be\na complete bust. It certainly a wait and see what the next few\nhours brings kind of a morning. Window for any storms today seems\nto close around or shortly after noon. \n\n\n- Extreme heat starts to set in today\n\nThe well advertised heat and humidity starts to build in today and\nremains through at least the end of the week. High temperatures \nshould reach the upper 80s to lower 90s today across West \nMichigan...making Monday the coolest day of the week. 90s to near\n100 for highs Tuesday through Thursday are still expected with\nheat index values of 105+. Lack of overnight relief from the heat\nand humidity still expected with lows in the 70s for at least the\nnext 4 nights.  \n\nIts possible we might see a few record highs this week...but we\nmay be more likely to break a couple of record warm low\ntemperatures.",
